Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='proposalreasons', at=datetime(2026, 9, 10, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='A proposal carries its reasons and can be answered no, behind the same Tap', body="*A proposal carries its reasons and can be answered no* (2026-09-10). `propose_email` requires `why` and `sources`; `secretary::store::Reasons` refuses either empty, deserialisation included, so a card always shows what the message is for and what it rests on. `POST …/proposals/<n>/dismiss` sits behind the SAME `Tap::of` (a `Tap` is a witness that the owner asked, not a permission to send, so answering is ONE gate; loopback mints neither). It records a `dismissed {reason, at}` outcome and a `Turn::Act` the secretary reads next round — an act, not a person's turn, because `thinking` is derived from the last turn and a person's would leave a page polling a model nobody started. `suzatary secretary dismiss` is the operator's twin; there is NO CLI twin of the tap.", rationale='Decided 2026-09-10.', supersedes=()))